The number 70 is chosen only for formatting the output. It creates a horizontal separator to make the console output easier to read.

For example:

print("=" * 70)
print("MARKET AGENT")
print("=" * 70)

Output:

======================================================================
MARKET AGENT
======================================================================
You can use any number

| Code               | Output                           |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------- |
| `print("=" * 10)`  | `==========`                     |
| `print("=" * 30)`  | `==============================` |
| `print("=" * 50)`  | 50 `=` characters                |
| `print("=" * 70)`  | 70 `=` characters                |
| `print("=" * 100)` | 100 `=` characters               |


